PANEL: Level complete. / CHAPTER 5 · THE DENIAL · ARCHIVE REVELATION / What the archive kept / 2,220 story points · 4 documents surfaced from this run / REPORT · MAY 2027 · INES MORENO / Internal memo: the Kessel spillway / To the Board. Our pipeline crosses the Kessel avalanche track. If the Kessel dam is overtopped, the flood follows that track. Option A: do nothing; our insurers will notice eventually. Option B: co-fund the spillway with the Water Board, at roughly what we spend on the annual shareholders' dinner (I checked). Option B also moves the tank farm up to the bench. I see the case for A: it is cheaper this year, and every year. I recommend B. I. Moreno / RECORD · JUNE 2027 · CALDER ENERGY / Calder Energy, board resolution 2027/14 / The board thanks the regional director for her memo. Resolved: to raise the bund around the Power Valley tank farm by one metre. Resolved: that co-funding public infrastructure is not the company's role. Resolved: to review the pipeline route at the next major maintenance, scheduled for 2041. / RECORD · SEPTEMBER 2024 · TOMAS LIND / Field notebook, the Kessel lake / Walked up to the Kessel lake with Anna. It has eaten the moraine on the left side and is twice the size I drew it in 1998. We stood and looked at it the way you look at an animal that has grown bigger than you were told it would. Anna said: it is not a lake, it is a budget line. I said: it is both. She wrote that down. / RECORD · MARCH 2025 · VELL VALLEY WATER BOARD / Water Board minutes, item 7 / Item 7: Kessel dam spillway. The Board noted the engineer's report and agreed with its conclusions. Following the withdrawal of national co-funding, the Board resolved to postpone the works to a future capital programme, to keep the matter under review, and to write to the Ministry. Action: Chair to write to the Ministry. Item 8: Christmas lights. / Kessel / You hit the Kessel dam with everything you had gathered on the way down, and it went, which is more or less what the 2024 report said would happen if something big enough arrived. I want to be fair to the people who read that report. They agreed with it. They minuted it. They wrote to the Ministry, and the Ministry wrote back very politely. A company director asked her board for the price of a dinner and got a raised bund instead. Denial is rarely anyone saying no. It is everyone saying yes, later. / From the archive · authored for this outcome / The run, as recorded / CONTINUE TO CHAPTER 6 / REPLAY CHAPTER / VIEW THE RIVER / CHAPTERS
